5,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I believe we should prioritize the human element. I'm interested in administrator retirements and hiring times, as well as depot supervisors and the last rollout, to see how our staff handles these transitions.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"That sounds like a great start, Misaki! I'm worried about the actual gear and timing on the floor. I want to check the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial, plus the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"I agree with the focus on stability. However, we must ensure the long-term financial commitment is transparent. I will look into the board minutes on capital and operating requests and five years of renewal invoices.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Yumi,,I think we should also look at how we handle trouble! I'll check support ownership during last winter's outage and warehouse rule changes after new accounts to see if we stay on track.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A comprehensive approach, indeed. To ensure we aren't simply polishing a sinking ship, I shall examine the data lift in the 2018 pay move and the upgrade history of the dispatch tool. Logic suggests stability lies in the details.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"It seems we have covered the financial, technical, and operational bases. I hope the data on our personnel reveals whether we actually have the capacity to implement a new system without burning out our remaining staff.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"I totally agree! But we also can't forget that the gear in the yards is pretty old. If the new system doesn't work with what we actually have on the floor, the staff will just be more stressed!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"Hardware is a factor, but the real risk is the budget. If we underestimate the recurring costs, the project will be viewed as a failure regardless of how the gear performs. We need a predictable cost model.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I totally get that! But if things break and nobody knows who's in charge, the costs will go up anyway, right? I just want to make sure we have a clear plan for when things get messy!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, a valid point. Chaos is rarely cost-effective. I suspect that if we find a pattern of fragmented updates or clumsy data migrations, we can better predict which vendors will offer a sustainable solution rather than a temporary patch.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. If the historical data shows a pattern of poor transitions, we must prioritize a vendor that offers extensive implementation support rather than just a feature-rich product. We cannot afford another rollout that fails on the ground.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! That's why I'm so focused on the peak-season cutover. If the timing is off, it doesn't matter how many features the software has—the freight still has to move! We need something that fits our real-world rhythm.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"The rhythm of the floor is important, but the rhythm of the budget is what sustains it. I want to see if our past spending matches the initial promises made to the board.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, you're so right about the budget! But I'm also worried that the plan we agree on now might not match our business in a few months. We need a system that can grow with us!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Growth is a noble goal, @Yumi, provided it isn't merely an accumulation of legacy errors. I am curious to see if our past ""growth"" was actually just a series of expensive repairs to outdated logic.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Misaki,,It seems we are all aligned on the need for a sustainable transition. I will stick with my choices to ensure we don't overlook the people who actually keep this company running.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
21,1,4,pass,Misaki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
22,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you, Misaki! I'll stick to my picks too. Let's find out if we can actually make this work in the yards without causing a total meltdown during peak season!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
23,1,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
24,1,4,talk,Toshio,,I will proceed with my selections. Understanding the gap between initial approvals and actual long-term expenditure is the only way to avoid hidden financial leakage. I look forward to the findings.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
25,1,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
26,1,4,talk,Yumi,,I'll stick with my choices too! I really hope we can find a way to make sure everyone knows their role and the system stays flexible. I'm excited to see what we find!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
27,1,4,pass,Yumi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
28,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall maintain my selections as well. It will be most illuminating to see if our history is one of genuine evolution or merely a collection of sophisticated bandages. I look forward to our subsequent analysis.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
