40,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"My findings are concerning. We are losing critical internal knowledge with two key administrators retiring, and hiring replacements is proving difficult. Furthermore, past rollouts show that standardized training is often ignored in favor of local routines.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, that sounds tough, Misaki! My news isn't great either. Our yard gear is a total mix of old models, and a previous trial failed because people just went back to using spreadsheets. It's a real mess out there!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings confirm a dangerous pattern. While capital requests are scrutinized, recurring operating costs are passed without question. Furthermore, separate licenses and add-ons have climbed yearly, creating a steady stream of hidden financial leakage.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh no, that's so stressful for everyone! My findings are scary too. Last winter, a big outage sat unowned for two days because four different suppliers just pointed fingers at each other! Nobody was actually in charge!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are painting a rather bleak portrait of our current state. My findings suggest a penchant for ""temporary"" fixes that become permanent burdens; we have skipped critical upgrades and suffered a year of data errors from outsourced work.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, the finger-pointing you mentioned is exactly what happens when the people on the ground are too stretched to manage vendors. If we don't have the staff to oversee the system, we'll be helpless during the next outage.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, you're right! And if the gear is old and the software is too fancy, the depot staff will just use spreadsheets again. We need a vendor who understands that our yards aren't perfect and our schedule is brutal!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, simplicity is a virtue, but it must be affordable. If we choose a vendor that seems ""simple"" but charges for every minor add-on, we will face the same escalating costs I found in the invoices.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree! But I also found that our warehouse rules had to be rewritten twice in one year because of new accounts. If the system is too rigid, we'll just end up paying for expensive changes anyway!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, precisely. Rigidity is merely a slower form of failure. Between the skipped upgrades and the lingering data errors from 2018, it appears we have a habit of inheriting problems we cannot solve. We must avoid another ""black box"" implementation.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, a ""black box"" is exactly what we can't afford. With our administrators retiring and hiring stalled, we won't have anyone left who knows how to open that box when things go wrong. We need transparency and heavy support.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, I'm with you! We need a partner who will actually come to the depots and help. If the system is too complex for the old gear or the peak rush, it's just a fancy paperweight!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, on-site support is a cost. We must be wary of vendors who offer ""partnership"" as a way to hide high hourly consulting fees. We need a flat, predictable cost structure that doesn't bleed us dry over time.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I understand, but isn't it more expensive to have a system that doesn't work? I'm really worried that if we don't have one clear point of contact, we'll just have more finger-pointing!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the cost of failure is indeed the highest expense of all. However, we must distinguish between a vendor who provides a solution and one who merely sells us a dependency. We cannot afford another cycle of outsourced errors.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We must prioritize a vendor that provides comprehensive, hands-on training and long-term support. Given our staffing crisis and the tendency for local depots to ignore standards, a ""set it and forget it"" approach will fail.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I totally agree! We need someone who knows that November to January is a no-go for big changes. If the vendor can't handle our peak-season chaos and our old scanners, they aren't the right fit for us!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I will prioritize a vendor with a bundled, all-inclusive pricing model. We cannot allow a system where ""hidden"" operating costs and add-on licenses quietly erode our budget while the board remains unaware. Predictability is non-negotiable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I'll be looking for a vendor who takes full ownership of the system so we stop the finger-pointing! We also need a flexible setup that can change as our business grows without breaking the bank!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall seek a vendor that prioritizes clean data migration and a sustainable update path. We must ensure the new system is an evolution, not merely a more expensive version of our current stagnation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
