64,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Given our staffing shortage and the failure of past training, Anchor Industrial Software seems best. Having an engineering team present through the rollout provides the hands-on support our overworked staff desperately needs.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with Misaki! Anchor sounds great because they'll actually be here on-site. If they're present during the rollout, they can see our old gear and help us survive the peak-season rush without everything crashing!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"I must disagree. Anchor's on-site engineering and server deployment likely hide significant long-term maintenance costs. Meridian Systems, with its hosted suite and fixed configuration, offers the predictability and bundled pricing we need to avoid financial leakage.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I see your point, but a fixed configuration sounds too rigid! Remember how our warehouse rules changed twice in one year? If we can't adapt, we're stuck. I think Tessera Cloud Suite's configurable workflows sound much more flexible!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, flexibility is a siren song if it leads to the same fragmented ownership we've suffered. Tessera's reliance on a partner firm for migration risks repeating the 2018 data disaster. I find Anchor's on-site presence more logically sound.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, predictability is useless if the system is abandoned by the staff. Meridian's fixed configuration won't stop depot supervisors from reverting to spreadsheets if the tool doesn't fit their reality. Anchor's on-site team can bridge that gap.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I get the money part, but if the system is too stiff, the guys in the yard will just ignore it! Anchor's team can actually see the old scanners and make sure things work before the November rush hits!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, @Misaki, on-site presence is a temporary comfort. Once the engineers leave, we are left with the bill for maintaining our own servers. Meridian's hosted model eliminates that hidden infrastructure cost and ensures a stable, bundled price.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, but if we have a problem, who do we call with Meridian? I'm so scared of that finger-pointing again! Anchor's team is right there, and Tessera's workflows can change with us. I'm leaning toward Tessera!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, Tessera's ""marketplace"" is a recipe for the very fragmentation we fear. It invites a patchwork of add-ons that will age unevenly. Anchor's on-site engineering ensures the logic is sound before it's left in our hands.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, the risk of finger-pointing is highest with a partner firm like Tessera's. Anchor's on-site team takes direct responsibility. With our administrators retiring, we need that immediate, physical support to ensure the system actually sticks.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, I'm really worried about that finger-pointing too! That's why Anchor is better than Tessera. If something breaks in the yard, we can just point to the engineer standing right there! It's the safest bet for us.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, that is a short-term solution to a long-term problem. Anchor's on-site presence is a luxury that will eventually transition into expensive support contracts. Meridian's hosted suite is the only option that guarantees a predictable, bundled cost structure.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I understand, but I can't ignore the risk of a rigid system! If we can't change the rules when new accounts arrive, we're just trading one problem for another. I still think Tessera's flexibility is a huge plus!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, flexibility without a central anchor is merely a path to chaos. @Toshio, while I appreciate your fiscal caution, the risk of a failed adoption is a far greater cost. Anchor's direct engineering presence is the most rational safeguard.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Misaki,,We cannot risk another rollout where the staff simply gives up. Anchor's on-site engineering is the only way to ensure the system is actually adopted despite our staffing crisis. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Misaki and Benjamin! We can't let the yard guys go back to spreadsheets because the software is too stiff or the support is far away. Anchor is the only one that fits our real-world chaos. I vote Anchor Industrial Software!,"{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I cannot support a model that relies on on-site engineering and internal servers, as it inevitably leads to escalating maintenance costs and budget leakage. Predictability is the only way to ensure long-term success. I vote Meridian Systems.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I really wanted flexibility, but @Misaki and @Kenji are right about the finger-pointing! I can't let that happen again. Anchor's on-site team gives me the most peace of mind. I vote Anchor Industrial Software!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is clear. To avoid the cycle of outsourced errors and stagnant systems, we must prioritize a successful implementation over a theoretical budget. Anchor's direct engineering presence is the most robust safeguard. I vote Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
